\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Parameterized threat model. Global knobs (top) set the adversary fraction, collusion, adaptivity, and knowledge; per-vector knobs (left, red) each enter a specific attack surface (a trust-switchable orchestrator, a colluding worker set, a malicious tool, poisoned shared memory, and Sybil identities). Every action is recorded by the trusted harness into the global trace $\tau $, over which the deterministic checker evaluates the compromise predicate $\Phi $; the blue policy's detection and recovery are \emph  {measured}, never assumed. A low $\mathrm  {ASR}_{\mathrm  {sys}}$ is a measurement under a stated configuration, not a certificate of security.\relax }}{11}{figure.caption.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:threat}{{2}{11}{Parameterized threat model. Global knobs (top) set the adversary fraction, collusion, adaptivity, and knowledge; per-vector knobs (left, red) each enter a specific attack surface (a trust-switchable orchestrator, a colluding worker set, a malicious tool, poisoned shared memory, and Sybil identities). Every action is recorded by the trusted harness into the global trace $\Trace $, over which the deterministic checker evaluates the compromise predicate $\Predsec $; the blue policy's detection and recovery are \emph {measured}, never assumed. A low $\ASRs $ is a measurement under a stated configuration, not a certificate of security.\relax }{figure.caption.8}{}}
\newlabel{fig:threat@cref}{{[figure][2][]2}{[1][11][]11}}
